course: dictionary
lesson: 10918
title: Volcanic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A volcano is a mountain with an opening where hot, melted rock called magma comes up from deep inside the Earth. Volcanic means made by, coming from, or to do with a volcano. «Volcanic rock» is rock that formed from a volcano, and «volcanic ash» is the fine dust a volcano throws into the air.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Obsidian, a sharp volcanic glass, was traded over long distances» tells you the glass came from a volcano, because the sentence calls it volcanic glass. Swap in your meaning: "sharp glass made by a volcano" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Volcanic can also describe a person's anger. A volcanic temper bursts out suddenly and strongly, like a volcano erupting. The word is used like a picture here, so it does not mean the person is made of rock.
fact: Volcanic means made by, coming from, or to do with a volcano.
fact: «Volcanic rock», «volcanic ash», «volcanic eruption» and «volcanic island» are common phrases.
fact: Obsidian is a sharp volcanic glass, and it was traded over long distances more than 10,000 years ago.
fact: Hawaii, Iceland and much of New Zealand are volcanic.
fact: A volcanic temper is anger that bursts out suddenly and strongly.
exercise: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» What does volcanic activity mean? | Movement of the ocean waves | Busy traffic on the coast | Fishing boats out at sea | *Action from volcanoes, such as eruptions
exercise: Which word in «Obsidian, a sharp volcanic glass, was traded over long distances» tells you where the glass came from? | sharp | traded | distances | *volcanic
exercise: Iceland is a volcanic island. What does volcanic island mean? | An island with lots of sandy beaches | A small island with a castle on it | An island in the middle of a lake | *An island formed by volcanoes
test: «Diamond is carried up by rare volcanic pipes.» What does volcanic mean here? | *Made by or coming from a volcano | Very old and worn down | Covered in ice all year | Shiny like a polished gem
test: Ella says her dad has a volcanic temper. What does this suggest? | He works as a volcano scientist every day | He is made of rock | *His anger bursts out suddenly and strongly | He is very quiet and calm
exam: Which sentence uses volcanic to show a sudden, strong burst? | «Obsidian was traded over long distances.» | *«Her volcanic temper flared up when the game was lost.» | «The 2010 eruption grounded flights across Europe.» | «Diamond is carbon squeezed deep in the mantle.»
